Q: What is Quarkus?

Quarkus is a **Kubernetes-native Java framework** (Red Hat) for building cloud microservices and serverless apps.
Tagline often used: “Supersonic Subatomic Java” → **fast startup + low memory**.

Designed so Java works well in containers: many small pods, quick scale-up/down, optional **GraalVM native images**.

────────────────────────────────────────
Core ideas

1) Build-time first
Heavy work (DI wiring, metadata, route discovery) happens at **build**, not mainly at runtime startup.

2) Standards-based APIs
- CDI (dependency injection)
- JAX-RS / Jakarta REST (REST)
- JPA / Hibernate (persistence)
- MicroProfile pieces (config, health, fault tolerance, etc.)

3) Extensions ecosystem
Like Spring Boot starters: add quarkus-rest, hibernate-orm-panache, redis, kafka, oidc...

4) Great Dev Experience
`quarkus:dev` → live reload, Dev UI.

────────────────────────────────────────
Typical stack pieces

| Concern        | Quarkus approach              |
| -------------- | ----------------------------- |
| REST           | Jakarta REST (`@Path`)        |
| DI             | CDI (`@Inject`, scopes)       |
| DB             | Hibernate ORM + Panache       |
| Config         | application.properties        |
| Reactive       | Mutiny (Uni/Multi) + Vert.x   |
| Security       | OIDC / JWT extensions         |
| Messaging      | SmallRye Reactive Messaging   |
| Ops            | /q/health, metrics            |

────────────────────────────────────────
Why companies adopt it

- Faster cold start than classic Spring Boot (esp. native)
- Lower RSS memory → denser Kubernetes packing / cost
- Container & serverless friendly
- Still “normal Java” skills (REST, DI, JPA)

────────────────────────────────────────
Interview one-liner

“Quarkus is a cloud-native Java framework that does much of Spring-like wiring at build time,
giving faster startup and lower memory — ideal for containers — while using CDI, JAX-RS, and Hibernate/Panache.”
